    {
      "text": "Undoped MnNiSi alloys display a strong magneto-structural transition.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The magneto-structural transition is responsible for the large magnetocaloric effect of MnNiSi alloys.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Undoped MnNiSi alloys have relatively limited mechanical robustness and lower mechanical strength.",
      "field": "material_initial_state; baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon added at approximately 0.2–0.5 at.% will occupy interstitial sites in the MnNiSi lattice.",
      "field": "hypothesis; intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interstitial carbon creates local lattice distortions in MnNiSi.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The carbon-induced lattice distortions impede or pin dislocations.",
      "field": "structural_mediator; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Trace interstitial carbon refines grain boundaries in MnNiSi-based alloys.",
      "field": "hypothesis; structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dislocation pinning and grain-boundary strengthening caused by carbon increase yield strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 0.2–0.5 at.% carbon will improve the mechanical performance of MnNiSi-based alloys.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon doping is expected to increase yield strength by roughly 20–30% relative to undoped MnNiSi.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Keeping the carbon content low will have minimal impact on the crystalline phase responsible for the magnetocaloric effect.",
      "field": "structural_mediator; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At low carbon content, the magneto-structural transformation will remain largely intact.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon-doped MnNiSi is expected to retain at least 90% of the undoped alloy's magnetocaloric entropy change.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Secondary carbide formation could disrupt the magneto-structural transition.",
      "field": "conditions; boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed benefit should hold only below approximately 0.5 at.% carbon and when processing prevents unintended carbide formation.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Minor processing deviations may alter the balance between mechanical and magnetocaloric properties.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
